From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wu <yuweiwu@pm.me>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:57:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Take the first font when it covers a cluster

FontSelector::select_font kept only whether the query yields a font with
a charmap (query_yields_font), so every cluster ran the query again:
fontique's family and attribute matching and each font's coverage. It
keeps that font instead (first_font), cleared where the flag was (a new
segment, a cluster of another family or emoji, other attributes), and a
cluster it fully covers takes it without the query. A cluster it doesn't
cover runs the query as before, so a missing glyph still falls back.

In a debug build every cluster taking the first font also runs the
query and checks it picks the same font: its data, index and synthesis.
